-Whereday offers one-time Individual Lifetime and Family Lifetime in-app purchases to unlock data portability features: in-app export in all formats, scheduled automatic exports, and webhook delivery. Eligible Individual Lifetime owners may purchase a separate one-time Family Upgrade. Family products use Apple Family Sharing, subject to the purchaser's Apple Family and Purchase Sharing settings. Owners of Whereday's original lifetime unlock receive Family Lifetime access without an additional charge. Tracking, the timeline, the Apple Watch app, and importing a prior export remain free. The App Store purchase sheet controls the displayed product, price, currency, tax, account, and Family Sharing eligibility. All purchases are processed through Apple and are non-refundable except as required by law or Apple's refund policies.
+### Existing access
+
+Users who first obtained Whereday before the subscription update keep their existing free tracking access. Existing free users retain their previous export-purchase requirement. Earlier lifetime purchases remain valid, including Family Sharing on the original lifetime unlock. No subscription is required to preserve this access. Apple purchase history and existing installation records determine eligibility; restoration may require the original Apple Account and a network connection. Contact support if prior access is not recognized.
+
+### New-user access from version 1.8
+
+Users who first obtain Whereday with the subscription update or later need an eligible subscription trial or valid purchase before starting tracking or adding manual visits. Individual and Family access are available as weekly subscriptions, yearly subscriptions, or separate one-time Lifetime purchases. There is no monthly plan.
+
+### Trials, payment, and automatic renewal
+
+Eligible weekly and yearly subscriptions offer a 7-day free trial. Apple determines eligibility within the subscription group; switching plans does not guarantee another trial. A trial starts only after you confirm with Apple. Lifetime purchases have no subscription trial.
+
+Unless canceled, subscriptions renew automatically at the price and interval shown by Apple before confirmation. After the trial, Apple charges the selected weekly or yearly price to your Apple Account. Local currency, applicable taxes, offer details, and plan-change billing are shown by Apple. Your account may be charged for renewal within the 24 hours before the current period ends.
+
+Manage or cancel in your Apple Account subscription settings. To avoid the next charge, cancel at least 24 hours before the trial or subscription period ends, or follow any earlier deadline shown by Apple for your offer/storefront. Deleting the app, stopping tracking, or removing permissions does not cancel billing. Access follows Apple's entitlement, expiry, and revocation status. Refunds follow Apple's policies and applicable law.
+
+### Lifetime purchases and Family Sharing
+
+Lifetime access is a separate one-time non-consumable purchase and does not renew. Existing lifetime purchases continue to cover their purchased features. An eligible Individual Lifetime owner can buy a separate Family Lifetime Upgrade. Buying Lifetime does not cancel an existing subscription; cancel that subscription separately to avoid unwanted renewal.
+
+Family products share eligible access with up to five other members through Apple Family Sharing, subject to Apple's settings, eligibility, and supported storefronts. Individual products are not family-shareable. Sharing access does not share anyone's location journal.
+
+### After access expires
+
+Users who joined under the subscription model can still view and export existing records after trial/subscription expiry, but cannot start new recording or add manual visits without active access. Expiry alone does not delete their records. Existing users retain their free tracking and earlier export requirements. Restoring purchases restores access, not deleted journal data.
+
+### Prices and refunds
+
+The App Store confirmation controls the product, price, currency, tax, and renewal terms. These terms do not announce a future price increase or guarantee a price across storefronts. Apple handles payments and refunds; contact Whereday support for access-recognition problems. Nothing here limits mandatory consumer rights.
 
